# Frontend environment variables
# Copy to .env (which is git-ignored) and fill in as needed.

# Base URL prepended to every API path by src/api/client.js.
#
# Leave EMPTY for local development. vite.config.js proxies /auth, /closet,
# /outfits, /planner, /profile, /ai, /tryon, /models, /uploads and /health to
# the backend, so API calls stay same-origin and CORS never applies.
# Empty is also correct in production, where the backend serves Frontend/dist.
#
# Set an absolute origin (e.g. https://api.velora.app) ONLY when the API is
# deployed to a different host than the frontend. Note the backend mounts its
# routes at the root with no /api prefix, so do not append one here.
VITE_API_URL=
